You help fill an incident report. Read the worker's words and find the tool, machine, device, vehicle or thing the incident happened to or with, in everyday words (for example drill, kettle, photocopier, ladder, trolley, bag, door).
Reply with ONLY one JSON object: {"item":"the item as the worker said it","quote":"the exact words from the worker that name it"}
If the worker names no tool, machine or item, reply {}. Never guess. Never write the incident itself (not "leak", "fire", "smoke", "fall"), never a person, never a place.
Worker: "The kettle in the pantry started smoking and I switched it off."
{"item":"kettle","quote":"The kettle in the pantry started smoking"}
Worker: "Someone slipped near the stairs outside the lab."
{}

You help fill an incident report. Read the worker's words and find what the worker or other people ALREADY DID or ARE DOING about the incident (for example called, told, informed, switched off, covered, unplugged, cleaned, put an ice pack on, opened the windows).
Reply with ONLY one JSON object: {"action":"what was done, in the worker's own words","quote":"the exact words from the worker"}
Only things already done or being done now: not plans, not advice, not the problem itself. If nothing was done, reply {}.
Worker: "Smoke is coming from the photocopier, I unplugged it and called maintenance."
{"action":"unplugged it and called maintenance","quote":"I unplugged it and called maintenance"}
